Caller evidence:

- Direct HTTP success/aggregate retained; added real createApiBridgeServer ->
  ephemeral HTTP adapter -> actual production chat POST -> real combo loop.
- Both gateway cases send auto/coding_high_tools:free, stream:false,
  max_tokens:64 and one lookup_status tool. Two distinct local free candidates;
  provider fetch only is mocked, not the combo or its final Response.
- Only former implicit native forwarding timeout 600000 is scaled to 250 ms;
  finite backend target timers remain 1500 ms. The second target is held behind a
  barrier: caller pending, no premature headers, application signal not aborted.
  Success returns exact assistant message and id; exhaustion returns backend
  HTTP 504 containing both dispatched model IDs and combo_target_timeout.
- Pretty JSON with trailing newline arrives byte-for-byte unchanged; actual
  seeded test authorization reaches the adapter and is passed to production POST.
- All three explicit forwarding inputs produce api_bridge_timeout 504 through
  real sockets using existing envs resolving to 100 ms, without timer scaling.
- Default noninference native forwarding remains 600000; existing responses,
  chat/completions and SSE-Accept path classification remains intact.
- Actual HTTP client abort after full body closes application connection,
  aborts provider signal, reaches terminal application completion with exactly
  one provider attempt (no later Auto dispatch). No timer scaling in this test.
- Resolver checks blank/invalid values, explicit max precedence and zero
  semantics; existing bridge peer-address/upgrade socket tests pass.

