## EX006 TEST-ONLY migration

Current fork-owned test paths:

- tests/unit/auto-fallback-http-response.test.ts: real bridge -> adapter -> production POST -> Auto/mock-provider response path.
- tests/unit/auto-fallback-request-lifetime.test.ts: 19 request-lifetime cases.
- tests/unit/fork-api-bridge-timeout-policy.test.ts: 37 assertions against the pure timeout resolver; default, all three explicit inputs, blank, invalid, zero and fractional values.

The original modified stock timeout test was restored byte-for-byte. No stock
test file or production source was changed by this migration. package.json's
unchanged top-level tests/unit/*.test.ts runner glob discovers the fork-api test.

Scoped verification command (Node's setup assigns isolated DATA_DIR per worker;
do not pass one shared DATA_DIR across files):
DISABLE_SQLITE_AUTO_BACKUP=true node --import tsx/esm --import ./open-sse/utils/setupPolyfill.ts --import ./tests/_setup/isolateDataDir.ts --test --test-force-exit --test-concurrency=2 tests/unit/fork-api-bridge-timeout-policy.test.ts tests/unit/auto-fallback-request-lifetime.test.ts tests/unit/auto-fallback-http-response.test.ts
Result: 35 tests, 35 pass, 0 fail, 0 skipped. Log: /tmp/omni-auto-ex006-policy-node-isolated.log.

An earlier invocation passed one shared DATA_DIR to all test workers and produced
2 failures in existing lifetime cases. That run is superseded; process isolation
restored by omitting DATA_DIR, after which all 35 tests passed. Its log remains at
/tmp/omni-auto-ex006-policy-node-pass.log. The first policy fixture run also had
an incorrect expected fallback for invalid REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS; the test now uses
the production module's 600000 ms fallback and passes 6/6 alone.

Retained prior report: strict-free Vitest 25/25 across three files and UI 3/3
(two default UI tests plus one strict-free UI test). These were verified before
this migration and were not rerun because their files and setup were unchanged.
The final five-file fork Node run is complete: 45/45 passed, zero failures,
